// UVM is a SystemVerilog class library. The shape, top to bottom:
//   test         picks the configuration and starts a sequence
//    env         holds agents, scoreboards, coverage collectors
//     agent      one per interface: sequencer + driver + monitor
//      sequencer arbitrates sequences competing for the driver
//      driver    turns transactions into pin wiggles
//      monitor   turns pin wiggles back into transactions (passive)
//     scoreboard compares monitored transactions to a reference model
//
// The three mechanisms that make it reusable:
//   factory     create by type name, so a test can substitute a
//               derived driver or transaction without editing the env
//   config_db   pass handles and settings down the hierarchy by
//               string path, so components need no constructor plumbing
//   phases      build -> connect -> run -> extract -> check -> report,
//               so every component's construction order is defined
//
// Free simulators cannot run UVM - it needs full class and
// constrained-random support. Routes that cost nothing: EDA
// Playground, Questa Intel FPGA Starter Edition, or pyuvm on cocotb.

L0.cloze:
// A UVM {{c1::agent}} bundles a sequencer, a driver and a monitor for one
// interface; the driver converts transactions into pin activity and the
// {{c2::monitor}} converts pin activity back into transactions independently,
// so the scoreboard never trusts the driver's view.
// The {{c3::factory}} lets a test substitute a derived class by type name
// without editing the environment, and the {{c4::config_db}} passes settings
// down the hierarchy by string path rather than through constructors.

