// Same language. Different economics. What actually changes:
//
//                     FPGA                      ASIC
//  power-up state     bitstream sets flops      undefined; needs reset
//  global reset       avoid; costs routing      required; async assert,
//                     and Fmax                  sync de-assert
//  memory             BRAM: fixed sizes,        compiled macros: any
//                     free, use the template    size, but not free
//  multiply           DSP48: 25x18, fixed       any width you pay for
//  clock gating       discouraged; use a        the primary dynamic
//                     clock-enable pin          power technique
//  latches            avoid                     forbidden outside
//                                               characterised cells
//  area unit          LUT/FF/BRAM/DSP counts    gates and microns
//  fixing a bug       rebuild, 20 minutes       a mask set
//
// Write for the stricter target: explicit resets, no initial values,
// no latches, no gated clocks in RTL. That code runs on both.

